Security Risk Team > Security and Technology Risk Management{#storm}

The Security Risk team provides risk management services including Security and Technology Operational Risk Management (STORM), AI Risk Management supporting our ISO42001 certification, and Unified Security Risk Management (USRM). These programs drive the identification, assessment, continuous monitoring, and reporting of Security and Technology Risks across the organization. Risk Reduction is one of the Security Division's operating principles (Security Vision and Mission). As such, the Security Risk Team takes a leading role in providing the information required by leadership to establish our Strategic Roadmap and support GitLab's key initiatives (internal only).

Please refer to the communication section of the STORM Program & Procedures page for information on the various ways that team members can use to escalate potential risks to the Security Risk Team.

Legal & Corporate Affairs ("LACA") > Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) Requests

The Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) provides public access to all United States federal agency records except for those records (or portions of those records) that are protected from disclosure by any of nine exemptions or three exclusions (reasons for which an agency may withhold records from a requester). Occasionally the records of a federal agency under a FOIA request may include GitLab records in the possession of the agency (i.e., when the agency is a customer of GitLab). In such an event, the federal agency will notify GitLab of the FOIA request and provide GitLab with the documents that the federal agency intends to release in response to the FOIA request. A GitLab legal team member will review the list and content of the documents identified by the federal agency pursuant to the FOIA request and will provide the appropriate response and/or make redactions to those documents, as necessary, prior to their release.

In the event you receive a notification from a US federal agency pursuant to a FOIA request, indicating that GitLab documents or information have been identified for release by an agency, please immediately forward the request to <FOIA@gitlab.com>.
